course: dictionary
lesson: 13944
title: Levitation: floating without support
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Levitation means rising or floating in the air with nothing visible holding you up. It is a noun for this action, and the verb is levitate. «The magician's levitation made the whole audience gasp.» The word gasp tells you the floating looked impossible, so levitation must mean something surprising and unusual.
explain: In stories, wizards and magicians use levitation to make people and objects float. Magic shows are pretend, though. Magicians use hidden tricks and illusions to make it look real. «The levitation trick looked real, but a hidden wire held the assistant up.» The wire was there, but the audience could not see it.
explain: Real levitation can happen in science, but there is always a force behind it. «The maglev train used magnets to float above its track.» Air or sound can also push things upwards. Nothing floats in the air for no reason, so when you read about levitation, always ask what is pushing or pulling.
fact: Levitation means rising or floating in the air with nothing visible holding it up.
fact: Levitation is uncountable: it has no plural, so we do not say «levitations».
fact: «Magnetic levitation» means floating because magnets push against each other, as on maglev trains.
fact: In magic shows, levitation is a trick that uses hidden wires, mirrors or illusions.
fact: Real levitation always has a force behind it, such as magnetism, air or sound.
exercise: «The magician's levitation made the whole audience gasp.» What does levitation mean? | Spinning very fast on one foot | Falling quickly to the ground | *Rising or floating in the air with nothing visible holding it up | Hiding something inside a hat
exercise: «The levitation trick looked real, but a hidden wire held the assistant up.» Is this real magic? | No, because the assistant was asleep | Yes, real magic made the assistant float | *No, it is a trick, and the hidden wire is the secret | Yes, because the audience gasped
exercise: In science, what can cause real magnetic levitation? | Nothing at all, it just happens | *A magnet pushing against another magnet | A wish made very hard | A wizard's spell
test: «The maglev train floated above its track because of magnetic levitation.» What is the force behind it? | A hidden wire | Wizard's magic | *Magnets pushing against each other | Nothing visible holding it up
test: Which word is the noun for the action? | levitating | *levitation | levitate | levitated
exam: Nadia says levitation is real magic in every show. What would you tell her? | Levitation means falling down quickly | Yes, every show is real magic | Levitation only happens to birds | *Most levitation on stage is a trick with hidden tools, but real levitation needs a force such as magnets
